[tool_use] Write {"file_path":"/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor/artifacts/phase-approval.json","content":"{\n  \"phase\": \"phase-2b.1\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"summary\": \"Phase 2b.1: LAN companion + WebRTC DataChannel transport with manual SDP paste. Shipped a typed wire contract (`app/src/phone/wire.ts`, PhoneMessage = `commit | ping`, encode/decode/isPhoneMessage with strict type-tag validation) and an RTCPeerConnection wrapper (`app/src/phone/peer.ts`, role-aware createOffer/acceptOffer/acceptAnswer/send/onMessage/onStateChange/close, default STUN stun.l.google.com:19302, peerConnectionFactory injection for tests). New `/phone` route on the same Vite SPA via a `/^\\\\/phone(\\\\/|$)/` test in `main.tsx`. PhoneApp (phone-side) ships paste-offer / generate-answer / Send-commit; PairScreen (laptop-side) ships generate-offer / paste-answer / Connect with a 'Last commit received at +Xms' debug surface that satisfies the §B2 testing-gate concession by giving manual QA a laptop-observable signal. Settings gained an optional `laptopLanIp` field that round-trips through Dexie and feeds the displayed phone URL; the 'Pair phone' button auto-saves before navigating so the PairScreen's `loadSettings()` read sees fresh state. vite.config.ts gained `server.host: true` and `preview.host: true` so the phone can reach the laptop on LAN. docs/QUALITY_GATES.md grew a 'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b)' footnote codifying the scoped testing-gate concession recorded in artifacts/decision-memo.md §B2. 25 new vitest tests (130 total, all green): 9 wire round-trip/rejection tests, 15 peer state-machine tests including a regression for the ondatachannel+onopen race during answerer ICE gathering, 1 settings round-trip test for `laptopLanIp`. Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Bundle 349.80 KB JS / 107.55 KB gzip (+2.26 KB gzip vs the Phase 5 baseline of 105.29; well under the +20 KB gzip budget). Reviewer (`code-reviewer`) returned APPROVE-WITH-CHANGES with one explicit conditional (manual_qa field populated; see review notes) plus seven non-blocking observations. The cheap correctness fixes were applied before approval: answerer race guard with regression test, exact-match /phone route, dropped unreachable port fallback, removed misleading removeEventListener cleanup that was a no-op for property-assigned handlers. Phase 2b.1's WebRTC transport handshake itself is gated by the manual_qa checklist (M1–M5 in `artifacts/phase-2b1-verify/results.json`) per the §B2 concession; the autonomous loop cannot perform real-device QA, so M1–M5 are recorded as `pending operator sign-off` in the approval artifact's `manual_qa` block — the operator (athlete on a real LAN with a phone) signs them off after this commit lands.\",\n  \"decision_memo\": \"artifacts/decision-memo.md\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"/phone route exists on the same Vite SPA (route swap in main.tsx)\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"verify-phase-2b1.mjs C1 — /phone renders PhoneApp with offer/answer textareas + state display. main.tsx uses /^\\\\/phone(\\\\/|$)/ test, exact-match per code-reviewer observation #4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Loading http://<laptop-lan-ip>:5173/phone on an Android phone on the same Wi-Fi renders PhoneApp\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"Automated: C1 confirms the /phone route renders PhoneApp from a Playwright origin. Real-device: M1 in manual_qa_checklist — pending operator sign-off.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Laptop 'Pair phone' screen renders the offer SDP in a textarea and accepts the answer SDP in another textarea\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"verify-phase-2b1.mjs C4 — Pair view exposes [aria-label='offer SDP'] (readonly), [aria-label='answer SDP'] (editable), [data-testid='pair-state'], and a phone-URL hint built from settings.laptopLanIp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Manual copy/paste of offer onto phone + answer onto laptop establishes a DataChannel within 5 seconds (verified via manual real-device QA)\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"Manual gate: M2–M4 in manual_qa_checklist — pending operator sign-off. Best-effort C5 in verify-phase-2b1.mjs runs two-context Playwright pairing on loopback; fails in headless chromium without UDP, which is the expected behavior documented under the §B2 concession.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Pressing the phone's 'Send commit' button echoes a `{ type: 'commit', t: number }` message that the laptop displays as 'Last commit at +Xms'\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"Unit: peer.test.ts asserts onMessage delivers a decoded {type:'commit',t:N} payload to subscribers, and PhoneApp.send uses peer.send → channel.send. PairScreen renders 'Last commit received at +Xms (phone clock t=...)' under [data-testid='last-commit']. Real-device: M5 — pending operator sign-off.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"SettingsRecord carries a new optional laptopLanIp field\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"settings-types.ts adds the optional field; settings.ts load/save round-trip it. settings.test.ts asserts the round-trip ('round-trips the optional Phase 2b.1 laptopLanIp field'). verify-phase-2b1.mjs C3 also asserts the IDB row carries laptopLanIp:'192.168.1.42' after a Save.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"phone/peer.ts and phone/wire.ts are unit-tested under vitest with stubbed RTCPeerConnection\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"peer.test.ts (15 tests) drives both offerer and answerer flows via FakePeerConnection, including STUN config, send/onMessage routing, single-role invariant, and the race-fix regression. wire.test.ts (9 tests) covers encode/decode round-trip and type-tag rejection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Lint + tsc + vite build clean. Bundle growth budget: +20 KB gzip\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"npm run lint: 0 errors. npm run typecheck: 0 errors. npm run build: 349.80 KB JS / 107.55 KB gzip (+2.26 KB gzip vs Phase 5 baseline of 105.29). Well within the +20 KB gzip budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Manual real-device QA documented at app/verify-phase-2b1.mjs + artifacts/phase-2b1-verify/results.json\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"verify-phase-2b1.mjs runs C1–C5 + writes results.json with the M1–M5 manual_qa_checklist. Current run: gate_checks_pass=true, c5_best_effort_pass=false (expected), console_errors=0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manual_qa\": {\n    \"device_used\": \"not_performed_by_agent\",\n    \"performed_by\": \"autonomous-agent\",\n    \"performed_at\": \"2026-05-26\",\n    \"playwright_run\": {\n      \"automated_gate_checks\": \"C1, C2, C3, C4 PASS — /phone renders, / renders main App, laptopLanIp round-trips through IDB (192.168.1.42), Pair view exposes form + computes phone URL.\",\n      \"best_effort_webrtc\": \"C5 FAIL — two-context headless chromium WebRTC handshake timed out, which is the documented expected outcome per QUALITY_GATES.md §'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b)'. This is not a gate failure; it is the rationale for the manual QA gate below.\",\n      \"console_errors\": 0\n    },\n    \"checklist_pending_operator_sign_off\": [\n      \"M1 — Phone on same LAN reaches http://<laptopLanIp>:5173/phone and renders PhoneApp.\",\n      \"M2 — Laptop 'Generate offer' button populates the offer textarea within 5s.\",\n      \"M3 — Phone 'Generate answer' populates the answer textarea within 5s after pasting the offer.\",\n      \"M4 — After pasting the answer back to the laptop and clicking Connect, both screens reach state='connected' within 5s.\",\n      \"M5 — Phone 'Send commit' causes the laptop to render 'Last commit received at +Xms' with X < 200.\"\n    ],\n    \"operator_sign_off_instructions\": \"Update artifacts/phase-2b1-verify/results.json — set each entry's `signed_off` to {date:'YYYY-MM-DD', device:'<phone model + OS>'} after exercising the step on a real LAN+phone pair. The §B2 concession requires this field to be populated before the phase can be considered fully closed; the autonomous loop cannot perform real-device QA, so the operator sign-off is the human's role in this gate.\"\n  },\n  \"gates\": {\n    \"testing\": \"130/130 vitest tests pass (Phase 5 baseline was 105; +25 new). Every new public behavior in wire.ts and peer.ts has at least one would-fail-if-reverted test; the race-fix regression test (peer.test.ts 'does not regress state to connecting if the channel opens during ICE gathering') gates the answerer state machine. Manual real-device gate per §B2 concession recorded in QUALITY_GATES.md and addressed in the manual_qa block above.\",\n    \"dry\": \"phone/peer.ts is the single source of truth for the RTCPeerConnection wrapper; both PhoneApp and PairScreen use it. wire.ts is the single source of truth for PhoneMessage shape; both ends import from it. Code-reviewer observation #5 (settings load/save field-list duplication) is pre-existing from Phase 4 and unchanged in shape by this phase — flagged for follow-up, not introduced here. PhoneApp/PairScreen duplication is intentional throwaway scaffolding per memo §'Throwaway scaffolding'.\",\n    \"drift\": \"No prior-phase invariants touched. RepRecord / SessionRecord / Dexie schema version unchanged. SettingsRecord widened by one optional field (`laptopLanIp?: string`) — additive, backward-compatible. ProfileRecord untouched. Phase 4 + Phase 5 functionality preserved (verified by 105 baseline tests passing alongside the 25 new ones).\",\n    \"planning\": \"decision-memo.md (Phase 2b decomposition) is the planning artifact. Phase 2b.1 acceptance criteria match docs/PHASES.md § Phase 2b.1 and the memo's §'Sub-phase 2b.1 — LAN companion-page + WebRTC DataChannel with manual SDP'.\",\n    \"verification_sprint\": \"Pre-phase: re-ran lint + tsc + 105/105 tests + vite build at the Phase 5 boundary before any 2b.1 code was added. Post-phase: 130/130 tests + lint + tsc + build all clean.\",\n    \"pre_commit_verify\": \"scripts/phasekit-verify.sh runs lint + typecheck + tests; all pass.\"\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"architecture_red_team\": \"Reviewed the Phase 2b decomposition in the prior iteration. Four blocking concerns (B1 LAN-trust model, B2 testing-gate concession, B3 falsifiable 2b.3 criteria, B4 Android-gated acceptance) resolved in artifacts/decision-memo.md before any 2b.1 code was written.\",\n    \"code_reviewer\": \"APPROVE-WITH-CHANGES on the implementation. Single conditional was manual_qa field population — addressed in the `manual_qa` block above with explicit operator-sign-off instructions. Seven non-blocking observations: (1) answerer race fix APPLIED with regression test, (2) waitForIceComplete listener-cleanup mismatch APPLIED (dropped no-op removeEventListener), (3) wire.ts validator shape DEFERRED to 2b.3 when new payload variants land, (4) exact-match /phone route APPLIED, (5) settings field-list duplication DEFERRED — pre-existing and unchanged in shape, (6) PhoneApp/PairScreen duplication ACCEPTED (intentional throwaway), (7) unreachable port fallback APPLIED (window.location.port is always present when the SPA is loaded).\",\n    \"qa_playwright\": \"Phase 2b.1 transport is gated by manual real-device QA per QUALITY_GATES.md §'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b)' — see manual_qa block. Automated UI gate checks C1–C4 in verify-phase-2b1.mjs all PASS with zero console errors; C5 best-effort WebRTC handshake fails under headless chromium without UDP, as documented and expected. Phase 4 + Phase 5 regression: not separately re-run this iteration; covered by the full vitest suite (130/130) which gates the analytics + drill + profiles modules unchanged in this phase.\"\n  },\n  \"suggested_commit_message\": \"phase-2b.1: LAN /phone route + WebRTC DataChannel transport + manual pairing UI\"\n}\n"}
