[result success] Phase 2b.1 approval written. The wrapper will pick up `artifacts/phase-approval.json` for commit. All gates passed:

- **Tests**: 130/130 (was 105; +25 new — 9 wire, 15 peer including a race regression, 1 settings).
- **Lint + tsc + build clean.** Bundle 349.8 KB JS / 107.6 KB gzip (+2.3 KB gzip vs Phase 5; budget +20).
- **Verify driver C1–C4**: PASS, zero console errors. C5 best-effort headless WebRTC: documented expected failure (handled by §B2 manual-QA gate).
- **Reviewer**: APPROVE-WITH-CHANGES. Cheap fixes applied: answerer race guard with regression test, exact-match `/phone` route, dropped misleading `removeEventListener` no-op, dropped unreachable port fallback. Single conditional (manual_qa field) addressed with explicit operator-sign-off instructions for M1–M5 since the autonomous loop cannot exercise WebRTC on a real LAN+phone pair.

